<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-3364] .NET: BinaryReflectiveSerializer raw mode does not work with DateTime fields</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-3364</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;BinaryReflectiveSerializer emits non-raw action for DateTime members when they are marked with &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;QuerySqlField&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is an unlikely scenario in production, since &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;QuerySqlField&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; does not make sense in raw mode. However, one of the users was experimenting with modes and encountered this issue.&lt;br/&gt;
The workaround is to implement IBinarizable in raw mode manually.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
